          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In general, a
            %em Freund-Rubin compactification
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#FreundRubin80"}> Freund &amp; Rubin 1980
            \&amp;rbrack; is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} Kaluza-Klein compactification
            of a theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            coupled to (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+field"}> higher
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"}> field strength
            ) on the compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            spaces such that the result is stable (a basic example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stabilization"} moduli stabilization
            via
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+compactification"} flux compactification
          %p
            One example are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactifications"} Kaluza-Klein compactifications
            of 6d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Maxwell+theory"} Einstein-Maxwell theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+flux"} magnetic flux
            on a 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            space (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#RDSS83"} RDSS 83
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+compactifications"} flux compactifications
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stabilization"} moduli stabilization
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            literature often
            %em the Freund-Rubin compactification
            refers by default to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} Kaluza-Klein compactification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_7
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            7 (in the original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            a round
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            (“flux”) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            in the remaining four dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetimes"} anti-de Sitter spacetimes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_4
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+AdS+spacetime"} super AdS spacetime
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_7
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+G%E2%82%82+holonomy"} weak G₂ holonomy
            with weakness parameter/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            the scale of the flux, then this yields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+QFT"} effective QFT
            in four dimensions, discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-reduction"} KK-reduction
            on the circle fiber of these solutions to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+supergravity"} type IIA supergravity
            yields type IIA sugra on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^3
            (
            %a{:href => "#NilssonPope84"}> Nilsson-Pope 84
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ABJM08"} ABJM 08
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_7 = S^7/G_{ADE}
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            of the round
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
            by an finite group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{ADE} \subset SU(2)
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-classification"} ADE-classification
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of coincident black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            at an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "M2-brane#AsABlackBrane"} M2-brane – As a black brane
          %h2#Details Details
          %h3#Preliminaries Preliminaries
          %p
            We work in the convention where a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/round+sphere"} round
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-sphere
            has
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+curvature"} scalar curvature
            (following
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FreundRubin80"} Freund &amp; Rubin 1980, below (4b)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Cartan+geometry#RiemannCartanGeometryOfS3"} this Example
          %p
            Notice that this means that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            appears with a
            %em positive
            sign on the
            %em right
            hand side of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein%27s+equations"} Einstein's equations
          %p
            For if we have an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+manifold"} Einstein
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+curvature"} Riemann curvature
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} R
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext hence
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} R
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msubsup
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R^{a_1 a_2}
                  \\;=\;
                  \\tfrac
                  { 2\, \mathrm{R} }
                  { D(D-1) }
                  \\,
                  e^{a_1}\, e^{a_2}
                  \\,,
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\text{hence}
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  R^{a_1 a_2}{}_{b_1 b_2}
                  \\;=\;
                  \\tfrac
                  { 2 \, \mathrm{R} }
                  { D (D-1) }
                  \\delta^{a_1 a_2}_{b_1 b_2}
                  \\,,
          %p
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ricci+curvature"} Ricci curvature
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ric
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≡
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mi c
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
